commit 22373959b781e9f1636e95b868df95005733d36d
Author: InnoPeak <global_ai@innopeaktech.com>
Date:   Wed May 20 11:40:51 2026 -0700

    fix(commands/finder, core-data tests): path authorization + negative contract cases (P1 D-group)
    
    Why
    - G3-E3 review (codex-reviews/g3-organizer-batch) flagged that `reveal_in_finder`
      and `open_path` only validated empty / NUL and accepted any absolute path,
      in violation of `docs/contracts/tauri-commands-v0.md` §4 "all path access
      must come from user drop/open panel or authorized bookmark".
    - G2.1 Repository v0 contract suite (`runRepositoryContractTests`) covered
      happy paths but lacked the documented `E3005` (invalid record) / `E3006`
      (migration version mismatch) negative cases and the `listByIndex` unknown-
      field shape, so neither driver was actually gated on the published contract.
    - The G3-batch commit `533391e` bundled five sub-features into one
      `feature-build` commit, deviating from the one-phase-per-run rule. The
      deviation needs to be recorded so Track A automation has a documented
      guard going forward.
    
    What
    - `apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/commands/finder.rs`
      - Replaced `validate_path` with `validate_user_path(raw) -> AppResult<PathBuf>`.
      - Rejects empty / whitespace-only / NUL (E3005), relative paths and any
        `..` component (E3005), and paths not under user-reachable roots
        (`/Users/`, `/Applications/`, `/Volumes/`, `/tmp/` on macOS; `/tmp/`
        only on other targets) with E3004.
      - Uses lexical normalization via `Path::components` (filesystem
        `canonicalize()` is deferred — it requires the path to exist on disk
        and a full bookmark store is a later gate).
      - Passes the normalized `PathBuf` to `open` / `open -R` instead of the
        raw input.
      - Added 4 cargo tests:
        `validate_user_path_rejects_dotdot`,
        `validate_user_path_rejects_etc_root`,
        `validate_user_path_admits_user_home`,
        `validate_user_path_admits_applications` (and updated existing tests
        to target the new function name).
    - `docs/contracts/tauri-commands-v0.md` §4
      - Replaced the two-row description for `reveal_in_finder` / `open_path`
        with the new path-shape contract ("non-empty / NUL-free / non-`..` /
        under user-reachable roots"). Documented the E3005 vs E3004 split and
        the lexical-normalization rationale. §6/§7 untouched.
    - `packages/core-data/tests/repository-contract.ts`
      - Added 3 negative contract cases (apply to every Repo<T> driver):
        - corrupted record (missing entityType / `schemaVersion=0`) → E3005;
        - migration plan with `fromVersion=5` against a fresh repo at
          migrationVersion=0 → `E3006: ... expected version`;
        - `listByIndex("nonExistentField" as never, "x" as never)` resolves
          to `[]`, not throwing or undefined, both empty-repo and populated.
      - Both `in-memory-repo.test.ts` and `sqlite-repo.test.ts` already invoke
        `runRepositoryContractTests`, so the new cases run against both drivers.
    - `packages/plugin-organizer/docs/dev_log.md`
      - Rewrote with a Status Panel reflecting current state (Workflow=FEATURE_DEV,
        Status=ACTIVE — multiple G3 features landed, Executor=Claude Code /
        Track A, Updated=2026-05-20 PDT).
      - Added a Work Log row per G3-batch sub-feature citing commit `533391e`
        and the Codex REVISE verdict, plus a row for this P1-Delta closure.
    - `docs/workflow/roadmap/codex-reviews/g3-organizer-batch/PROCESS-NOTE.md`
      - New file. Documents the G3-batch deviation acceptance (5 sub-features
        bundled into `533391e`), the forward guard ("future sub-feature batches
        MUST be split per the one-phase-per-run rule"), and the carry-forward
        P1/P2 closure table.
    
    Scope
    - apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/commands/finder.rs
    - docs/contracts/tauri-commands-v0.md (§4 only — §6/§7 untouched)
    - packages/core-data/tests/repository-contract.ts
    - packages/plugin-organizer/docs/dev_log.md
    - docs/workflow/roadmap/codex-reviews/g3-organizer-batch/PROCESS-NOTE.md (new)
    - DO NOT TOUCH: keychain.rs / database.rs / window.rs / menubar.rs / crypto/ /
      @repo/core / plugin-organizer/src/ / @repo/core-data/src/.
    
    Risk
    - Behavior change for `reveal_in_finder` / `open_path`: any caller passing
      a path outside the four allowed roots will now receive E3004 instead of
      the OS-level `open` exit code. This is the intended hardening; callers
      must route through drag-drop / open-panel / authorized bookmark.
    - `/private/var/...` is intentionally rejected for now — the `/var → /private/var`
      macOS symlink dance means a future bookmark resolver may want to widen
      the allow-list, but for P1 we keep the conservative set.
    - Lexical normalization (not `canonicalize()`) means a symlink under one of
      the allowed roots is still admitted; tightening this is the bookmark-store
      follow-up.
    - Repository contract negative tests are additive — no production code
      change; both `createInMemoryRepo` and `createSqliteRepo` already throw
      the right error codes via `assertRepoRecord` / `assertMigrationPlan`.
    
    Docs
    - `docs/contracts/tauri-commands-v0.md` §4 updated (rules + error codes +
      rationale).
    - `packages/plugin-organizer/docs/dev_log.md` — Status Panel + Work Log
      rows for the G3-batch and the P1-Delta closure.
    - `docs/workflow/roadmap/codex-reviews/g3-organizer-batch/PROCESS-NOTE.md`
      — deviation acceptance + carry-forward table.
    
    Tests
    - `cargo test --manifest-path apps/desktop/src-tauri/Cargo.toml finder::`
      → 7 passed / 0 failed (includes the 4 required new tests).
    - `cargo check --manifest-path apps/desktop/src-tauri/Cargo.toml`
      → clean (5 pre-existing unrelated dead-code warnings).
    - `pnpm --filter @repo/core-data test`
      → 72 passed / 0 failed across 7 test files; in-memory + sqlite drivers
        both exercise the 3 new negative-path cases.
    - `pnpm --filter @repo/core-data check-types`
      → clean (tsc --noEmit).

